Z||000003||Oreif||05-13-2001||09:58 PM||||Now is the time to install a killer sound system.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Is the car going to be ready for the Village Pontiac Car Show on June 24th?<P>If you need help let me know.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||05-13-2001||10:31 PM||||If you've ever wanted some power options that you dont have, now is the time to do it.  When I had my interior out, I added:<P>power door locks<BR>Power mirrors<BR>Power trunk release<BR>Circuit to use defogger switch to turn on/off driving lights<P>Timer circuit for EL Scanner (triggered by door locks, now replaced with 555 IC circuit)<P>Keyless entry/alarm system with many goodies (ignition controlled locks, dome light illumination, trunk pop, shock sensor)<P>Performance sound system w/overhead controls<P>underseat switch panel to control all my electrical goodies without having to drill holes all over dash (2 buttons, 2 switches)<P>I think that's about it!  I love having a lot of buttons and switches to play with!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||05-13-2001||11:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Now is the time to install a killer sound system.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Is the car going to be ready for the Village Pontiac Car Show on June 24th?<P>If you need help let me know.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Oreif,<BR>  The sound system will be going in the '88.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Ill have to stop by soon & we can take some measurements. <P>I decided to do the interior because I'm getting ready for the Village Pontiac Car Show. I was going to bring the '85 to the Dells but I have too much work to do on it. Ill let ya know if I run into any problems. Im doing the headliner right now.  <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>If you've ever wanted some power options that you dont have, now is the time to do it.  When I had my interior out, I added:<P>power door locks<BR>Power mirrors<BR>Power trunk release<BR>Circuit to use defogger switch to turn on/off driving lights<P>Timer circuit for EL Scanner (triggered by door locks, now replaced with 555 IC circuit)<P>Keyless entry/alarm system with many goodies (ignition controlled locks, dome light illumination, trunk pop, shock sensor)<P>Performance sound system w/overhead controls<P>underseat switch panel to control all my electrical goodies without having to drill holes all over dash (2 buttons, 2 switches)<P>I think that's about it!  I love having a lot of buttons and switches to play with!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>FieroJoe,<BR>  I'm full power with the exception of mirrors. (I don't want to install those) I have an custom Pontiac emblem where the power mirror switch would be) Thanks for the ideas though...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">      </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
